  "id": "Compound::DB01628 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Etoricoxib, a selective COX-2 inhibitor, is shown to bind to Cyp2d6 and Cyp2e1, both of which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are known to catalyze the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid, a process that generates bioactive lipid mediators. The observed pathway links Etoricoxib to Cyp2c19 through the shared involvement of arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Etoricoxib may influence Cyp2c19 function. The evidence is supported by the consistent binding of Etoricoxib to Cyp2d6 and Cyp2e1, and the subsequent involvement of these enzymes in the same metabolic pathway as Cyp2c19. This indicates that Etoricoxib may modulate Cyp2c19 activity through a shared metabolic pathway involving arachidonic acid epoxygenase. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a final score of 0.6386, suggesting a plausible and well-supported relationship between Etoricoxib and Cyp2c19.",
